33,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I found out that some rooms get no sun and need heat way earlier! And people were actually sweating it out in summer to avoid arguments!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The bills are incredibly volatile. February was nearly three times the cost of August. Also, fitting sub-meters would cost 34,000 yen per room plus annual fees.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,Oh no! The other house spent forty minutes just logging readings! And the template for the year-end settle looked like a total nightmare of typing!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"My suspicions were correct. One person's usage is roughly four times another's, mostly due to heaters and desktops. The payment log also shows frequent late payments.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,The payment log confirms that queries about changing amounts lead to delays. It also took three weeks just to agree on the newcomers' first payments.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, four times the usage?! That's huge! No wonder people are scared to turn on the heat. It feels unfair if some of us are freezing!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, that is the problem with a flat split. However, @Rin's findings suggest that the administrative burden of precise metering is significant.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,It really is! I don't want us to spend our whole evening doing math or typing into templates. That sounds so boring and stressful!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, the cost of the electrician is high, but the ""social cost"" of the current system is higher. People are paying for others' desktops and heaters.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, the late payments and arguments prove that the current lack of transparency is damaging our relationships. We need a system that stops the queries.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"But if we just divide it by five, will the people in the cold rooms still feel bad? I don't want anyone wearing a coat inside!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"A flat split is simple, but as Shunichi noted, the usage gap is extreme. Yet, the upfront cost for meters is a heavy burden for everyone.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Misaki, if we make it too complicated, won't we just argue more about the math? I want something that just... works!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, ""just working"" usually means someone is being cheated. If we ignore the usage gap, the resentment will only grow.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi, I agree. But we must balance precision with peace. If the system is too tedious, the person managing it will become the villain.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,I just want us to be able to use the heater without feeling guilty or worried about the bill!,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"We have a conflict between financial precision, upfront cost, and administrative labor. We must weigh these carefully when we see the options.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'm voting for whatever is the least amount of work! I can't stand the thought of those forty-minute reading sessions!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I'll be looking for the option that most accurately reflects actual consumption. Fairness should be based on data, not convenience.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I will support the option that minimizes conflict and removes the need for constant, awkward reminders and queries.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
