60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Okay, let's look at the options! A is a seasonal fixed rate, B is per-room metering, and C is a flat household share.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option B is too expensive upfront and has high maintenance. Option C is the simplest but ignores the usage disparity I saw in the statements.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,Option B sounds like that forty-minute nightmare I read about! And Option C might still lead to arguments if the total jumps around!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option C is exactly what we have now, just updated for five people. It doesn't solve the problem of one person carrying the others.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option C is the most likely to cause the ""queries"" and late payments I found in the logs because the monthly amount is unpredictable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"What about Option A? If we have a fixed rate for the season, we don't have to worry every time we flick a switch! That sounds so relaxing!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A provides budget stability, which I value. It avoids the high cost of meters while smoothing out the winter spikes.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mio, if it's a fixed rate, does that mean no more monthly math headaches? If we just pay one amount, that sounds way better!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Option A is a compromise. It doesn't perfectly track usage like B, but it's more stable than C. However, the year-end settlement could be a mess.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Rin, yes, it would reduce the monthly friction. As long as the year-end settle is handled simply, it removes the monthly accusation cycle.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,I love Option A! No more sitting in a coat in February just to save a few yen. I'm voting for A!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"It is the most rational balance. It avoids the 34,000 yen per room fee of Option B and the volatility of Option C. I vote A.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm with Mio! No boring math every month and no expensive meters. Option A is the winner for me! I vote A!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"While not as precise as B, it's a significant improvement over C. It prevents the monthly ""who used what"" arguments. I vote A.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,Option A removes the unpredictability that sours our communication. It's the best choice for the harmony of the house. I vote A.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,Yay! We all agree! Now we can all be warm and happy this winter!,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,It is a sustainable decision. The financial predictability is a major advantage for all of us.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,No more math monsters! I'm so happy!,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,A rare moment of total consensus. Let's hope the year-end settle is handled with a bit more maturity than the current system.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I'm glad we could find a solution that prioritizes our relationships. I'm happy with this result.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
